  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="36466e3f-7526-5a2f-8c6c-b432b37af10d" activityNameId="8fce66a5-aa4a-541d-a808-1f3ee54b7519" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Rail, at regional storage</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Rail, at regional storage
The inventory refers to the production of 1 kg of rail. The data for the manufacture of rails was mainly taken from the information in Table 3.14 in (Messmer &amp; Frischknecht, 2016). This includes the rail and the associated steel elements of the support. Only the breakdown between primary and secondary steel was updated with information from SBB (pers. comm., SBB, 2024). The proportion of secondary steel is currently 60 % and is likely to increase further in the future. 
Offcuts and rejects are not taken into account. The ecoinvent standard values were used for transport distances of material deliveries by lorry (Frischknecht et al., 2007) 
According to SBB, the service life of such a track is 25 years. Maintenance work, refurbishment and dismantling of the rail are not taken into account.; UUID:0997435b-c105-30ad-8320-1f28033fbb13
The inventory includes all the materials, energy and transport necessary to manifacture 1kg of rail. Excluded are maintenance and disposal
Location: Data apply to construction in Switzerland. 
Technology: Average technology available on the market
Time period: Time of publications.
Production volume: 
Sampling: based on literature 
Extrapolations: none
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_0997435b-c105-30ad-8320-1f28033fbb13.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
